{"answer": "No. Lore's auto-merge loop fixes nothing. Its merge-ready decision (`decideMergeReady`) returns only \"ready\" or \"wait\". If a pull request's CI is red, the loop waits. The loop that opened the pull request is responsible for repairing it. The old fixer pieces (`auto-merge-fix`, `fix-pr`, `fix-replies`) were deleted in PR #3376 on 2026-10-23. Since then, the implementation loop keeps its own pull requests mergeable. When a loop PR is behind main, conflicted or red, an \"upkeep run\" starts at the `sync-pr` entry in response to GitHub push and check_suite events. A person's PR is left for that person to fix.", "sources": ["apps/stations/src/work/pr-ready-check/decide-merge-ready.ts", "memory: session-summary/2026-10-23-loop-pr-upkeep-auto-merge-no-fixer (PR re-cinq/lore#3376)", "apps/stations/src/events/loop-upkeep-handlers.ts"]}
